#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Writes this case's fixture data into the run's workspace (both arms see the same files).
# Generated by benchmarks/builder; edit the case script there, not this file.
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p resources
cat > resources/free_shipping_test_readout.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Free shipping test: readout

Kestrel Tea Co. growth team, draft for the leadership meeting

## Setup

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| Dates | 1 to 14 September 2026 (14 days) |
| Split | 50 / 50, tool: SplitWise, assignment unit: session_id |
| A (control) | Current site: $5.95 flat shipping on every order |
| B (variant) | Free shipping on all orders, "Free shipping, always" header bar, express checkout button (one-tap wallet pay) on the cart page |
| Primary metric | Conversion rate: converting users / users |

Note from the tool: 8.4% of users were assigned to both A and B on different sessions; they are counted in both arms.

## Result

| Arm | Users | Converting users | Conversion rate |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | 90,212 | 2,991 | 3.32% |
| B | 89,874 | 3,215 | 3.58% |

Lift: **+7.9%**, z = 3.04, p = 0.0023. Sample ratio check passed (90,212 vs 89,874, p = 0.43).

Randomisation check: two of six variables are imbalanced (cart adds per user and pages per session, both higher in B, p < 0.05; see balance_check.csv). B seems to have drawn more engaged shoppers by chance, so to be conservative we discount the lift by 2.5 points to **+5.4%**.

7 September: the payment provider had a 5-hour outage. Both arms were affected; we kept the day in.

## What it is worth

At the current order value ($68) and our monthly traffic, the extra orders are worth about **$88,458 a month** in revenue.

## Recommendation

Roll out free shipping sitewide from 1 October. Free shipping is the single biggest conversion lever we have tested this year.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
